24:<g class="state-path rollback"><rect x="10" y="386" width="244" height="76" rx="9"/><text x="29" y="416" class="node-title">Equal capture time</text><text x="29" y="439" class="node-copy">New ingestion key, stale data</text><path d="M255 424H322" class="chart-arrow"/><rect x="329" y="386" width="345" height="76" rx="9"/><text x="348" y="416" class="node-title">Error and rollback</text><text x="348" y="439" class="node-copy">Revert every attempted mutation</text><path d="M675 424H737" class="chart-arrow"/><rect x="746" y="386" width="320" height="76" rx="9"/><text x="765" y="416" class="node-title">Database unchanged</text><text x="765" y="439" class="node-copy">Compared as a complete snapshot</text></g></svg></div><p class="state-explanation">The regression compares complete database snapshots for retries and rollback, including row IDs, timestamps, and the ingestion ledger. <a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading/tests.rs#L172">Read the transaction test</a>.</p></section><section id="findings" class="section"><h2>Where proof still stops</h2><div class="coverage-alerts"><article><h3>No full declaration chain</h3><p>Capture, real scoring, loading, and HTTP have separate checks. No single test exercises all stages together.</p><a href="#reach">Compare the proof paths</a></article><article class="warn"><h3>Resolution drive has policy drift</h3><p>The script expects policy v2. The backend emits v3. If the drive reaches that assertion, it cannot publish a success proof.</p><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/.agents/skills/verify/scripts/resolution.py#L125">Inspect the stale assertion</a></article><article><h3>Real Splink CLI test is opt-in</h3><p>It uses the actual clean and resolve binaries and pinned worker, but Cargo ignores it by default. Python worker tests call scoring directly.</p><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/declaration_resolution_cli.rs#L46">Inspect test selection</a></article><article class="warn"><h3>Legacy suite has collection drift</h3><p>A test imports a missing SQL upgrade. Legacy database adapters also require term tables absent from the current baseline.</p><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/tests/test_funder_upgrade.py#L20">Inspect the legacy import</a></article></div></section><details id="reference" class="reference"><summary>Detailed assertions, source links, and run recipes</summary><p>47 behavior groups cover current Rust tests, CLI verification, direct Python scoring, and legacy Python intent. Filter the reference to inspect one area.</p><section id="coverage" class="section"><h2>Covered behavior</h2><p class="section-intro">Each row groups related assertions. Expand its evidence to inspect the tests and their limits. The number of groups is not a code-coverage percentage.</p><form class="controls" id="filters" role="search" aria-label="Filter behavior coverage"><div class="query-control"><label for="query">Find a behavior or source</label><input id="query" type="search" placeholder="Try rollback, alias, HTTP, or a test name"></div><div><label for="stage">Pipeline stage</label><select id="stage"><option value="">All stages</option><option value="members">Members</option><option value="capture">Capture</option><option value="clean">Cleaning</option><option value="resolve">Resolution</option><option value="load">Database load</option><option value="http">Search &amp; details</option><option value="schema">Schema</option><option value="operations">Operations</option></select></div><div><label for="suite">Evidence family</label><select id="suite"><option value="">All families</option><option value="rust">Rust tests</option><option value="verification">CLI verification</option><option value="worker">P