25:<section id="gaps" class="section"><h2>Coverage gaps and runner drift</h2><p class="section-intro">These are source-inspection findings. A missing assertion is different from a failing implementation; runner drift prevents the affected proof from completing as written.</p><div class="gap-grid"><article class="gap blocker"><h3>Stale resolution verification policy</h3><p>If the drive reaches line 125, its v2 assertion conflicts with emitted v3. Repeat checks and proof writing occur later. No failure was observed by executing the runner.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/.agents/skills/verify/scripts/resolution.py#L125" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/.agents/skills/verify/scripts/resolution.py:125</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/domain/models/declaration_resolution.rs#L10" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/domain/models/declaration_resolution.rs:10</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>No test spans the full declaration pipeline</h3><p>No single automated real pipeline reaches fetch→clean→real Splink→load→HTTP.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/declaration_resolution_cli.rs#L48" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/tests/declaration_resolution_cli.rs:48</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading/tests.rs#L39" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading/tests.rs:39</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/entity_details/tests.rs#L14" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/entity_details/tests.rs:14</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>HTTP search rejection and error paths</h3><p>Search query rejection/default strictness and search DB-error responses lack targeted HTTP assertions; existing HTTP suite asserts happy search ID only.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/inbound/http/handlers.rs#L27" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/inbound/http/handlers.rs:27</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/inbound/http/handlers.rs#L70" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/inbound/http/handlers.rs:70</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/entity_details/tests.rs#L180" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/entity_details/tests.rs:180</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>Live capture lacks deterministic pagination tests</h3><p>Live API pagination executes with Take=5 but page count, exhaustive completeness, empty intermediate pages, malformed/error responses and duplicate handling lack deterministic HTTP adapter tests.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/parliament_api/declarations.rs#L14" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/parliament_api/declarations.rs:14</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/common/mod.rs#L93" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/tests/common/mod.rs:93</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/integration.rs#L99" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/tests/integration.rs:99</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>Live members test leaves cohort completeness unasserted</h3><p>parliament_api_parses_all_sitting_members only asserts first John McDonnell search result; does not assert all sitting members parsed or expected cohort count.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/integration.rs#L51" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/tests/integration.rs:51</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/integration.rs#L92" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/tests/integration.rs:92</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>HSBC smoke check leaves identity merging unasserted</h3><p>shows_no_hsbc_duplicates checks each spelling occurs once, not that all aliases resolve to a single entity/identity; requires ambient preloaded DB and two-second startup sleep.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/integration.rs#L30" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/tests/integration.rs:30</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/common/mod.rs#L56" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/tests/common/mod.rs:56</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>Worker-failure test stops at scorer error</h3><p>worker_process_failure_does_not_publish_or_fake_scores invokes only scorer; proves error includes Python exception, not resolution publication behavior.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_resolution/tests.rs#L36" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_resolution/tests.rs:36</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>Loader integrity and concurrent-load cases</h3><p>Loader manifest/hash/count corruption, identity/pair/attribution mismatch, missing raw partitions, same-key changed fingerprint, absent/mismatched member and concurrent loader lock have implementation checks without targeted Rust tests.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs#L68" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs:68</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs#L78" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs:78</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs#L93" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs:93</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs#L191" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs:191</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs#L225" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs:225</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs#L633" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs:633</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs#L641" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs:641</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs#L682" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/declaration_loading.rs:682</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>Alias-only funder search</h3><p>Alias-only funder search is implemented but repository tests query canonical fixture names; no dedicated assertion exercises alias matching.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/funder.rs#L29" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/funder.rs:29</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/funder.rs#L90" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/funder.rs:90</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap gap"><h3>Member refresh and database failure paths</h3><p>Member upsert errors/transaction rollback and existing member refresh lack targeted tests; implementation prints individual SQL errors and continues.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/parliament_member.rs#L82" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/parliament_member.rs:82</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/outbound/parliament_member.rs#L119" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/src/lib/outbound/parliament_member.rs:119</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/tests/integration.rs#L51" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exposed/tests/integration.rs:51</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap blocker"><h3>Legacy pytest imports a missing SQL upgrade</h3><p>test_funder_upgrade imports absent db/upgrades/normalize_funders.sql at module import, causing FileNotFoundError during collection even without DSN.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/tests/test_funder_upgrade.py#L20" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ingest/tests/test_funder_upgrade.py:20</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap blocker"><h3>Legacy adapter expects obsolete term tables</h3><p>Python member pipeline needs exposed.parliament_terms and member_terms; current baseline/upgrades lack both. Integration tests cannot validate modern schema even after bypassing missing upgrade.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/src/exposed/adapters/postgres.py#L27" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ingest/src/exposed/adapters/postgres.py:27</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/src/exposed/adapters/postgres.py#L32" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ingest/src/exposed/adapters/postgres.py:32</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/src/exposed/adapters/postgres.py#L83" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ingest/src/exposed/adapters/postgres.py:83</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/tests/test_importer.py#L26" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ingest/tests/test_importer.py:26</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/db/migrations/20260915000000_initial.down.sql#L2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">db/migrations/20260915000000_initial.down.sql:2</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap blocker"><h3>Missing Makefile invalidates documented recipes</h3><p>README make db-start/check/test-unit and Makefile-supplied admin DSN claims are stale: no Makefile in current repository. Linked recorded verification/member-import.md also missing.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/README.md#L172" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ingest/README.md:172</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/README.md#L179" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ingest/README.md:179</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/ingest/README.md#L181" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ingest/README.md:181</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/db/README.md#L14" target="_blank" rel="noopener">db/README.md:14</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/db/README.md#L30" target="_blank" rel="noopener">db/README.md:30</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap blocker"><h3>Funder-upgrade guide references a missing file</h3><p>db README still instructs applying missing normalize_funders.sql. Current resolved loader upgrade is a different script; legacy tests do not cover that current upgrade.</p><ul class="evidence-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/db/README.md#L104" target="_blank" rel="noopener">db/README.md:104</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/db/README.md#L162" target="_blank" rel="noopener">db/README.md:162</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/db/README.md#L168" target="_blank" rel="noopener">db/README.md:168</a></li></ul></article><article class="gap blocker"><h3>SQL diagnostic has no automated assertions</h3><p>verify.sql is a manual SELECT diagnostic, not automated assertion. 