32:<section id="method" class="section"><h2>How this report was assembled</h2><div class="method"><ul><li>Reviewed current source and explorer inventories at the recorded snapshot.</li><li>Counted Rust test functions statically; macro categories describe runners rather than integration boundaries.</li><li>Grouped assertions by behavior and cited corresponding test functions or runner assertions.</li><li>Separated pure domain policies, fake ports, real artifacts, PostgreSQL, TCP HTTP and actual Splink boundaries.</li><li>Validated every cited source path and line exists; no backend execution or percentage claim.</li></ul><p>The 88 Rust entries are source functions carrying <code>#[test]</code>, <code>#[tokio::test]</code>, or <code>#[sqlx::test]</code>. Loops, fixtures, assertions, and parameter permutations do not count as extra test functions. Attribute categories are not substitutes for integration boundaries.</p><p>The browser-facing frontend tests are outside this backend audit. Findings describe this revision and can drift when tests or policies change.</p></div><details class="inventory"><summary>Complete Rust test-function index (88 entries)</summary><p class="section-intro">50 ordinary test attributes, 23 Tokio attributes, and 15 SQLx attributes. Follow a name to its declaration in the audited source.</p><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Test function</th><th scope="col">Source file</th><th scope="col">Attribute</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/domain/models/declaration_resolution/tests.rs#L69" target="_blank" rel="noopener">exact_donor_names_link_without_address_or_threshold</a></td><td><code>exposed/src/lib/domain/models/declaration_resolution/tests.rs</code></td><td>#[test]</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/blob/7009ffa7ad3e7fd0445a95456d08726d97c44a29/exposed/src/lib/domain/models/declaration_resolution/tests.rs#L1